    "description": "The org holds three generations of Operator/Partner Accounts. Only the client's real upload carries an external ID.\n\n**Rule applied:** has an external ID → keep. No external ID → test data, delete.\n\nSurvivors: **58 Operators** (OP-00064..00121) + **5 Partners** (PT-CTM, PT-C, PT-D, PT-DIRECT, PT-GD).\n\n## Done 2026-08-20\n\n* 19 Accounts stamped `Operational_Notes__c` = MARK FOR DELETION (11 Operator, 8 Partner).\n* 9 sample Deals remapped to the surviving Accounts.\n* 21 Sign-Ups remapped (11 direct, 10 OLG repointed onto new Deals + DRAs).\n\n## Still to do\n\n1. **Decide OLG and iRival** — neither is on the client upload list, so there is no replacement record. They hold 5 sample Deals (SAMPLE-DEAL-003, -007, -008, -010, -011). Recommend deleting those Deals outright; they are July test data.\n2. Delete DRAs on those 5 Deals first — `DRA.Deal__c` is `deleteConstraint=Restrict`, the Deal delete fails while children exist.\n3. Delete the 5 Deals.\n4. Delete the 19 Accounts.\n\n**Do not reorder.** `Operator__c` is a required lookup on Deal.\n\n## Before deleting — easy to lose\n\n`Operator_Aliases__c` (e.g. \"BetMGM Casino MI/NJ;BetMGM Casino PA\") exists **only** on the records being deleted. If the CMS will ever match operators by alias, migrate that data to the surviving records first. Not recoverable afterwards.",
